    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Data Sufficiency asks a different question.\n\nYou are not mainly asked to solve the tank problem. You are asked whether the information is enough to solve it.\n\nSo first ask: what rate information do I actually need? Then test each statement on its own.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Question: How long to empty a tank when inlet A and outlet B are both open?\nI. A fills in 16 min.\nII. B empties in 8 min.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "I alone gives only +1/16. II alone gives only −1/8.\nTo find the net rate, both are needed.\nTogether net emptying = 1/8−1/16 = 1/16, so the tank empties in 16 min.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
